- SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Televised address by Federal Chancellor Olaf Scholz on the Russian attack against Ukraine","publisher":"Federal Government","publication_date":"2022-02-24","url":"https://www.bundesregierung.de/breg-en/service/archive/televised-address-by-federal-chancellor-olaf-scholz-on-the-russian-attack-against-ukraine-2007846","claim":"Scholz described Russia's attack on Ukraine as unjustified aggression, said Germany had pursued diplomacy before the invasion, and announced sanctions while insisting the conflict must not spread.","locator":"lines 150-205","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct contemporaneous statement by the Chancellor on the official federal website.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact start-of-war response in 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Direct Scholz statement and federal policy position.","contrary_evidence":["The speech pairs condemnation with sanctions and deterrence rather than immediate negotiated settlement.","It is a public justification, not proof that all alternatives were exhausted."],"lenses":["2B.1","2B.2","2B.3","2B.6","2B.10"]}
- SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"In policy shift, Berlin to deliver defensive weapons to Ukraine","publisher":"Euronews / Reuters","publication_date":"2022-02-27","url":"https://www.euronews.com/2022/02/27/us-ukraine-crisis-germany-defence","claim":"Germany shifted policy to supply Ukraine with defensive anti-tank weapons, Stinger missiles, and ammunition, with Scholz calling Russia's invasion a turning point and saying Ukraine should be able to defend itself.","locator":"lines 664-667","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters wire reporting with direct contemporaneous attribution and clear policy details.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Immediate 2022 invasion response.","ruler_attribution":"Cabinet-level decision under Scholz; the quote is directly attributed to him.","contrary_evidence":["It marks a break from prior restraint on arms exports to war zones.","It supports defense, but also widens Germany's military involvement in the war."],"lenses":["2B.1","2B.3","2B.10"]}
- SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Federal Government commits to additional aid","publisher":"Federal Government","publication_date":"2022-05-05","url":"https://www.bundesregierung.de/breg-de/aktuelles/ukraine-donors-conference-2037428","claim":"At a donors' conference, Scholz pledged an additional 125 million euros for humanitarian aid and said the funds were also intended to increase Ukraine's ability to defend itself against Russian aggression.","locator":"lines 189-191 and 217-223","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official government summary with direct attribution to the Chancellor and conference context.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022 war-period policy support.","ruler_attribution":"Direct Scholz pledge, under federal executive authority.","contrary_evidence":["Humanitarian aid is peace-supportive, but the same package also reinforces wartime defense.","It does not by itself show a negotiated peace strategy."],"lenses":["2B.4","2B.7","2B.10"]}
- SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Germany's Scholz pushes for Ukraine ceasefire in call with Putin","publisher":"Reuters / Investing.com","publication_date":"2022-05-13","url":"https://uk.investing.com/news/commodities-news/germanys-scholz-pushes-for-ukraine-ceasefire-in-call-with-putin-2648262","claim":"Scholz urged Putin to agree to a ceasefire as soon as possible, saying a truce was needed to improve the humanitarian situation and allow progress toward a diplomatic solution.","locator":"lines 422-425","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters wire reporting on a direct government-spokesperson account of the call.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022 crisis diplomacy.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to Scholz's call with Putin through the government spokesperson.","contrary_evidence":["This is a ceasefire push, not a verified breakthrough.","The report does not show Russian acceptance or concrete de-escalation results."],"lenses":["2B.1","2B.7","2B.10"]}
- SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Human Rights Commissioner Luise Amtsberg on today’s publication of the report produced under the OSCE’s Moscow Mechanism documenting violations of international law and human rights in Ukraine","publisher":"Federal Foreign Office","publication_date":"2022-04-13","url":"https://www.auswaertiges-amt.de/en/newsroom/news/amtsberg-report-osze-2522892","claim":"Germany said the OSCE Moscow Mechanism report documented severe breaches of international humanitarian law and human rights, possible war crimes, and targeted killings and abductions of civilians, and that Germany would help ensure accountability.","locator":"lines 101-110","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official foreign-office statement summarizing an independent expert report and Germany's response.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022 wartime accountability context.","ruler_attribution":"Government-level attribution under Scholz's chancellorship.","contrary_evidence":["This is support for investigations, not direct command over battlefield conduct.","It relies on an OSCE expert report rather than a German operational record."],"lenses":["2B.4","2B.9"]}
- SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Joint statement on Ukraine’s application against Russia at the International Court of Justice","publisher":"Federal Foreign Office","publication_date":"2022-05-20","url":"https://www.auswaertiges-amt.de/en/newsroom/news/2532254-2532254","claim":"Germany joined a statement welcoming Ukraine's ICJ case, saying Russia had no lawful basis for military action, urging compliance with the ICJ's order to suspend military operations, and endorsing accountability and peaceful settlement.","locator":"lines 98-106","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary diplomatic/legal statement with Germany named among the signatories.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022 legal-diplomatic response.","ruler_attribution":"Government-level attribution under Scholz; not a private or military act.","contrary_evidence":["The statement supports lawfare and accountability, not a direct ceasefire.","It is multilateral and not unique to Scholz's personal initiative."],"lenses":["2B.4","2B.7","2B.9","2B.10"]}
- SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Sanctions will not be lifted until Russia signs peace deal with Ukraine - Germany's Scholz","publisher":"Euronews / Reuters","publication_date":"2022-05-03","url":"https://www.euronews.com/2022/05/03/uk-ukraine-crisis-germany-scholz","claim":"Scholz said sanctions imposed after the invasion would stay until Russia reaches a peace agreement with Ukraine and Germany would not accept Russia's annexation of Crimea.","locator":"lines 610-614","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters wire reporting with direct attribution and clear date-specific policy content.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022 sanctions and settlement stance.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to Scholz as head of government.","contrary_evidence":["The policy preserves pressure rather than quick compromise.","It rejects territorial revision, but does not itself produce peace talks."],"lenses":["2B.2","2B.7","2B.9","2B.10"]}
- SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Putin will not dictate Ukraine peace terms: Scholz","publisher":"Euronews / Reuters","publication_date":"2022-05-27","url":"https://www.euronews.com/2022/05/27/us-davos-meeting-scholz","claim":"Scholz said Russia would not win the war, rejected a dictated peace, and insisted that Ukraine, not Russia, must decide the terms of any agreement.","locator":"lines 664-671","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters wire reporting from a public Scholz speech with direct quotations.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022 war and peace-dispute period.","ruler_attribution":"Direct Scholz public position.","contrary_evidence":["It rejects coercive settlement, but also commits to continued Western support.","It does not show a negotiated result or a ceasefire gain."],"lenses":["2B.1","2B.7","2B.10"]}
- SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Germany to send Ukraine arms for as long as needed - Scholz","publisher":"Euronews / Reuters","publication_date":"2022-06-22","url":"https://www.euronews.com/2022/06/22/uk-ukraine-crisis-germany-arms","claim":"Scholz said Germany would continue sending weapons to Ukraine for as long as Ukraine needed support.","locator":"lines 608-610","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters wire reporting of a direct public statement by the Chancellor.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Mid-2022 wartime policy.","ruler_attribution":"Direct Scholz statement.","contrary_evidence":["This can be read as prolonging military support rather than pushing a quick settlement.","The report itself gives no endpoint or peace framework."],"lenses":["2B.1","2B.7","2B.10"]}
- SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Ukraine security guarantees will not be same as for NATO member - Scholz","publisher":"Euronews / Reuters","publication_date":"2022-07-04","url":"https://www.euronews.com/2022/07/04/us-germany-politics-scholz-ukraine","claim":"Scholz said Germany and its allies were discussing security guarantees for Ukraine after the war, but they would not be the same as NATO membership guarantees.","locator":"lines 668-670","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters wire report of a direct broadcast interview with the Chancellor.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022 postwar-security discussion.","ruler_attribution":"Direct Scholz statement about allied policy.","contrary_evidence":["The guarantees are prospective and undefined.","The statement is cautious and does not commit Germany to a concrete settlement architecture."],"lenses":["2B.7","2B.10"]}
- SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Speech by Olaf Scholz, Chancellor of the Federal Republic of Germany and Member of the German Bundestag, at the 77th general debate of the United Nations General Assembly","publisher":"Federal Government","publication_date":"2022-09-20","url":"https://www.bundesregierung.de/breg-en/service/archive/speech-by-olaf-scholz-2128554","claim":"Scholz said Russia's war of occupation against Ukraine had no justification, rejected a dictated peace, and framed continued support for Ukraine with weapons, sanctions, and diplomacy as necessary to uphold the UN order.","locator":"lines 189-216 and 232-241","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct contemporaneous Scholz speech in the official federal archive.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact late-2022 international posture.","ruler_attribution":"Direct Scholz rhetoric and government policy signaling.","contrary_evidence":["The speech supports arming Ukraine, which is not pure de-escalation.","It relies on broad political framing rather than a concrete peace agreement."],"lenses":["2B.1","2B.2","2B.6","2B.7","2B.10"]}
- SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Rede von Bundeskanzler Olaf Scholz bei der Konferenz zum Wiederaufbau der Ukraine am 25. Oktober 2022 in Berlin","publisher":"Federal Government","publication_date":"2022-10-28","url":"https://www.bundesregierung.de/breg-de/service/newsletter-und-abos/bulletin/rede-von-bundeskanzler-olaf-scholz-2138928","claim":"Scholz called for a peaceful, prosperous, and resilient Ukraine, said Germany and partners would keep supporting Ukraine with political, financial, humanitarian, and military means, and presented reconstruction as a long-term international task.","locator":"lines 198-214","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct Scholz speech in the official bulletin archive.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact end-of-2022 posture.","ruler_attribution":"Direct Scholz statement and hosting role.","contrary_evidence":["The speech treats military aid and reconstruction as parallel, not separate, tracks.","It is forward-looking and does not prove conflict termination."],"lenses":["2B.7","2B.10"]}

Search and rejection summary
- I reviewed roughly 30 documents across German federal archives, the Foreign Office, Bundestag/OSCE/ICJ material, and Reuters-wired reporting hosted by Euronews or similar outlets.
- I kept the documents that actually moved 2B: war justification and diplomacy on 24 Feb, arms and ceasefire policy in spring and summer 2022, humanitarian and legal-accountability actions, and the late-2022 reconstruction posture.
- I rejected later 2023-2026 archive pages when they mainly restated the same 2022 policy without adding target-period nuance.
- I rejected nuclear-risk pages and procurement pages that were useful for 1B but not materially for 2B.
- I rejected broad Ukraine-support summaries when they were updated long after 2022 and did not add a distinct Scholz-specific 2022 claim.
- I rejected duplicate translations or syndicated copies when they repeated the same Reuters text without adding a new material claim or locator.

Remaining gaps
- Public evidence is thin on internal cabinet deliberations, especially the tradeoff between caution and escalation in spring 2022.
- The record shows Scholz's public position clearly, but less clearly shows what Germany could have done differently at each decision point.
- A few useful items are multilateral or government-level rather than uniquely Scholz-personal, so attribution is strong but not perfectly individualized.
- More search would help only marginally unless you want a deeper file on Bundestag debate records, cabinet minutes, or contemporaneous peace-process reporting.
